quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  106,1,"To awake drive amongst the Quraysh,"
  106,2,They were acclimatized to the summer and winter (commercial) trips.
  106,3,"So they should worship the Lord of this (Sacred) House (Ka‘ba, to give Him thanks),"
  106,4,"Who has fed them in hunger (i.e., provided them sustenance in starving conditions) and secured them from fear (of foes i.e., blessed them with secure and peaceful life)."
  107,1,Have you seen him who denies the Din (Religion)?
  107,2,"So he is the one who pushes away the orphan (i.e., rejects the needs of the orphans and deprives them of their right),"
  107,3,"And does not promote the cause of feeding the poor (i.e., does not strive to end the economic exploitation of the poor and the needy)."
  107,4,"So woe to those worshippers,"
  107,5,"Who are unaware of (the spirit of) their Prayers (i.e., they are mindful only of the rights of Allah, but are heedless of the rights of fellow human beings),"
  107,6,"Who show off (their worship, for they only render a formal service to the Creator and are inconsiderate to the oppressed humanity),"
  107,7,And who refuse to lend a worthless small object of use even on demand!
  108,1,"Indeed, We have bestowed on you an infinite abundance (every kind of superiority, bliss and bounty).*"
  108,2,So pray to your Lord and offer sacrifice (a token of gratitude).
  108,3,"Indeed, your enemy will remain childless and his race will be cut off."
